{"summary":"Both amendments identify real test-quality regressions. The first test is mathematically tautological and does not exercise the production nitrogen-cycle path, and the second test was weakened enough that it no longer validates the actual diagnostic payload for the renamed field.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-6-49d40a08","decision":"accept","rationale":"In `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs`, `per_guild_monod_uses_concentration_not_total` only computes totals from a concentration and volume, divides by the same volume, and then compares `monod` on the reconstructed value to `monod` on the original concentration. That is an identity check, not a behavioral test. It never calls `step_nitrogen_cycle` or another production helper that could regress to total-mass-based K_s handling, so the amendment correctly identifies a false sense of coverage."},{"amendment_id":"fr-6-01ebb675","decision":"accept","rationale":"In `crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs`, `loader_range_diagnostics_use_explicit_warning_lines` now asserts only that one warning exists and that it contains a generic prefix. Given that `RangeWarning` formatting includes the parameter name, value, and range, dropping those checks means a warning for the wrong field or with incorrect payload would still pass. Restoring assertions on the actual warning content for `aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l` is the correct fix."}]}